BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-kossoikia-panigiri-at-the-castle-of-koskina-agios-georgios-d-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270902
SUMMARY:Panigiri at the Castle of Koskina (Agios Georgios Dorganas)
LOCATION:Kossoikia\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 1 September the Panikarian Riding Club 'Agios Georgios Dorganas' hosts a panigiri below the Byzantine castle of Koskina\, the rocky peak above Kossoikia in the centre of the island\, with Nikos Kochylas 'Ounga' and his orchestra\, goat (proto) and wine from midday. Unusual setting\, a short but steep walk from the parking at the foot of the hill. Wear shoes for the rocks.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#kossoikia-panigiri-at-the-castle-of-koskina-agios-georgios-d
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#kossoikia-panigiri-at-the-castle-of-koskina-agios-georgios-d
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kasos-agios-mamas-monastery-apokrani-panigiri-of-agios-mamas-apokr-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270903
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Mamas\, Apokrani monastery
LOCATION:Agios Mamas monastery (Apokrani)\, Kasos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 1-2 September pilgrims head to the monastery of Agios Mamas\, perched on a cliff above the Libyan Sea south of the island: vespers\, then lamb offered by the shepherds\, roasted and served with pilaf\, dolmadakia and fried potatoes to 400-plus people by a chain of volunteers\, with the Perselis family playing the old Kasiot tunes. Many stay overnight in the monastery cells. The road is rough\; a 4x4 or a lift from a local helps.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#agios-mamas-monastery-apokrani-panigiri-of-agios-mamas-apokr
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#agios-mamas-monastery-apokrani-panigiri-of-agios-mamas-apokr
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skyros-ai-mamas-panigiri-of-agios-mamas-ai-mamas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270903
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Mamas\, Ai-Mamas
LOCATION:Ai-Mamas\, Skyros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The shepherds' saint gets one of the last big feasts of the Skyrian summer on 1-2 September at the chapel of Ai-Mamas\, with goat and pilaf tavles and music through the night\; September is when the island empties of tourists and the panigiria are at their most local.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skyros/#ai-mamas-panigiri-of-agios-mamas-ai-mamas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skyros/#ai-mamas-panigiri-of-agios-mamas-ai-mamas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:spetses-spetses-town-dapia-feast-of-agios-mamas-and-blessing-of-the--2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270903
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Mamas and blessing of the horses\, Dapia
LOCATION:Spetses Town (Dapia)\, Spetses\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The tiny chapel of Agios Mamas stands on the beach by the Dapia\, built by a captain saved from a storm in 1850 while carrying grape must\; on the evening of 1 September\, after vespers\, the island's horse-carriages line up and the priest blesses the horses and their drivers\, and the story of the vow is retold. Ten minutes\, free\, and one of the most Spetsiot things you can see\; it falls the week before the Armata.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#spetses-town-dapia-feast-of-agios-mamas-and-blessing-of-the-
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#spetses-town-dapia-feast-of-agios-mamas-and-blessing-of-the-
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:aegina-kontos-agios-nektarios-feast-of-the-translation-of-the-relic-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270902
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270904
SUMMARY:Feast of the Translation of the Relics of Agios Nektarios\, Agia Triada Monastery
LOCATION:Kontos (Agios Nektarios)\, Aegina\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Besides his main feast on 9 November\, Aegina's saint has a second\, summer one: on 2 September there are vespers at 7 pm at the monastery of Agia Triada\, a procession of the relics to the big church\, and an all-night vigil from 10 pm to 5 am\; on the 3rd the liturgy and a second procession with relics and icon at 10.30 am. The Dimos lays on extra buses from the port\; if you want to sleep in a guesthouse near the monastery\, book weeks ahead.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/aegina/#kontos-agios-nektarios-feast-of-the-translation-of-the-relic
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/aegina/#kontos-agios-nektarios-feast-of-the-translation-of-the-relic
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:astypalaia-chora-feast-of-osios-anthimos-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270902
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270904
SUMMARY:Feast of Osios Anthimos\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Astypalaia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The island's patron\, the monk Anthimos who brought the Portaitissa icon\, is honoured on 3 September with a liturgy and procession through Chora. A quiet\, local occasion at the end of the season.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/astypalaia/#chora-feast-of-osios-anthimos-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/astypalaia/#chora-feast-of-osios-anthimos-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:serifos-agios-sostis-livadi-panigiri-of-agios-sostis-agios-sostis-be-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270906
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270908
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Sostis\, Agios Sostis beach
LOCATION:Agios Sostis (Livadi)\, Serifos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:A beach chapel feast on the little isthmus of Agios Sostis\, a short drive or a 40-minute walk from Livadi: vespers on the evening of 6 September\, fava and goat from the ktitores and wine on the sand\, liturgy at dawn on the 7th. September water is at its warmest\, so people swim before and after. Parking is a handful of spaces on the track — walk if you can.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#agios-sostis-livadi-panigiri-of-agios-sostis-agios-sostis-be
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/serifos/#agios-sostis-livadi-panigiri-of-agios-sostis-agios-sostis-be
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:anafi-panagia-kalamiotissa-pilgrimage-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panagia Kalamiotissa pilgrimage
LOCATION:Anafi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Two-day pilgrimage to the chapel atop Mount Kalamos (460m) — a vertical limestone monolith on the island's east coast\, second only to Gibraltar in Mediterranean profile. Pilgrims walk up overnight\; an all-night service ends with sunrise above the Aegean. The most spectacular small-island pilgrimage in Greece.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/anafi/#panagia-kalamiotissa-pilgrimage
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/anafi/#panagia-kalamiotissa-pilgrimage
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:andros-vitali-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiri-vitali-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Nativity of the Virgin panigiri\, Vitali
LOCATION:Vitali\, Andros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The beach hamlet of Vitali on the north-east coast holds the last panigiri of the Andros summer on 8 September\, with a liturgy at the chapel of the Virgin and food\, wine and music by the sea. Reached by a long dirt road from Vourkoti or Ano Agios Petros\; go with a car you do not mind scratching.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#vitali-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiri-vitali
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/andros/#vitali-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiri-vitali
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:antiparos-faneromeni-south-antiparos-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-by-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Faneromeni (by boat)
LOCATION:Faneromeni\, south Antiparos\, Antiparos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The whitewashed chapel of Panagia Faneromeni on the wild southern tip of Antiparos can only be reached by caique or a long dirt track\, and on 7-8 September the whole island goes out there for the Nativity of the Virgin with food and wine after the liturgy. Ask at the harbour a day or two ahead about boats leaving for the feast.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/antiparos/#faneromeni-south-antiparos-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-by
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/antiparos/#faneromeni-south-antiparos-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-by
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:astypalaia-poulariani-east-astypalaia-panigiri-of-panagia-poulariani-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Poulariani
LOCATION:Poulariani (east Astypalaia)\, Astypalaia\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Nativity of the Virgin is kept at the cave chapel of Panagia Poulariani on the eastern arm of the island beyond Vathy\, with vespers on the 7th and a small feast with violins after. Reached by dirt road or boat from Vathy\; ask locally about lifts.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/astypalaia/#poulariani-east-astypalaia-panigiri-of-panagia-poulariani
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/astypalaia/#poulariani-east-astypalaia-panigiri-of-panagia-poulariani
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:chios-chalkeios-feast-of-panagia-leiapyrgousaina-chalkeios-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Feast of Panagia Leiapyrgousaina\, Chalkeios
LOCATION:Chalkeios\, Chios\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The country chapel of Panagia Leiapyrgousaina near Chalkeios\, south of Chios town\, keeps the Nativity of the Virgin with festive vespers at 19:00 on the eve and matins\, bread-blessing and liturgy from 07:00 on 8 September. The Nativity is also kept the same day in Pityos\, Lithi\, Elata\, Leptopoda and other villages\; this one is the closest to town.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chios/#chalkeios-feast-of-panagia-leiapyrgousaina-chalkeios
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/chios/#chalkeios-feast-of-panagia-leiapyrgousaina-chalkeios
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:heraklion-agios-thomas-panigiri-of-panagia-karkadiotissa-agios-thomas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Karkadiotissa\, Agios Thomas
LOCATION:Agios Thomas\, Crete (Heraklion)\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:For the Nativity of the Virgin the Messara village of Agios Thomas walks out to the 14th-century chapel of Panagia Karkadiotissa by the river for vespers on the evening of 7 September\, followed by a glenti\; it is the last big panigiri of the Heraklion season. The chapel is a short walk from the village\; bring a torch for the way back.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#agios-thomas-panigiri-of-panagia-karkadiotissa-agios-thomas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/heraklion/#agios-thomas-panigiri-of-panagia-karkadiotissa-agios-thomas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:hydra-zourva-feast-of-panagia-zourva-monastery-8-september-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Feast of Panagia Zourva Monastery (8 September)
LOCATION:Zourva\, Hydra\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The women's monastery of the Nativity of the Theotokos at Zourva\, on the far eastern tip of Hydra\, keeps its feast on 7-8 September with vespers on the eve and a liturgy with a representative of the Metropolitan. It is a two-hour walk from town over the ridge or a water taxi to the cove below\; the nuns offer coffee and sweets\, and September is the best month to do the path.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/hydra/#zourva-feast-of-panagia-zourva-monastery-8-september
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/hydra/#zourva-feast-of-panagia-zourva-monastery-8-september
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ios-agia-theodoti-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiri-agia-theodoti--2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Nativity of the Virgin panigiri\, Agia Theodoti and Paleokastro
LOCATION:Agia Theodoti\, Ios\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 7-8 September the church at Agia Theodoti beach and the chapel of the Virgin inside the Byzantine fort of Paleokastro both celebrate the Nativity of the Virgin\, with vespers\, a shared meal and music. Paleokastro is a steep 20-minute climb from the road\, so most people go to Agia Theodoti in the evening and up to the castle for the morning liturgy.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#agia-theodoti-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiri-agia-theodoti-
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ios/#agia-theodoti-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiri-agia-theodoti-
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ithaca-kathara-monastery-above-perachori-feast-of-panagia-kathariot-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Feast of Panagia Kathariotissa\, Kathara Monastery
LOCATION:Kathara Monastery (above Perachori)\, Ithaca\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Nativity of the Virgin is the feast of Ithaca's patron icon at the Kathara monastery\, 600 m up above Vathy: great vespers on the evening of 7 September\, hierarchical liturgy on the 8th with the Metropolitan of Lefkada and Ithaca\, and a meal offered to pilgrims by the monastery. Come for the view from the bell tower as much as the service\; the road up from Perachori is paved but slow.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#kathara-monastery-above-perachori-feast-of-panagia-kathariot
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ithaca/#kathara-monastery-above-perachori-feast-of-panagia-kathariot
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:karpathos-mesochori-panigiri-of-panagia-mesochoritissa-mesochori-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Mesochoritissa\, Mesochori
LOCATION:Mesochori\, Karpathos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Mesochori\, a car-free village of stepped lanes on the west coast\, celebrates the Nativity of the Virgin at Panagia Mesochoritissa\, the church built over the village spring\, with vespers on the 7th and a feast with lyra and laouto on the square. Volada also feasts on 8 September. Park at the top of the village and walk down.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#mesochori-panigiri-of-panagia-mesochoritissa-mesochori
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/karpathos/#mesochori-panigiri-of-panagia-mesochoritissa-mesochori
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kasos-ellerou-monastery-panigiri-of-panagia-ellerou-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Ellerou
LOCATION:Ellerou monastery\, Kasos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Nativity of the Virgin is kept at the isolated monastery of Panagia Ellerou in the island's interior\, where families still use the old shepherds' cells (mitata) around the church to sleep over. Vespers on the 7th\, then food\, wine and dancing. Ask in Fry about lifts\; there is no bus.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#ellerou-monastery-panigiri-of-panagia-ellerou
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kasos/#ellerou-monastery-panigiri-of-panagia-ellerou
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kos-kardamena-panigiri-of-genesio-tis-theotokou-kardamena-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Genesio tis Theotokou\, Kardamena
LOCATION:Kardamena\, Kos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kardamena's parish feast on 7-8 September is the one night the resort belongs to the locals: vespers at the Panagia church\, then a glendi with island music on the square. In early October the same village holds its smelt (marida) festival with free fried fish by the harbour.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#kardamena-panigiri-of-genesio-tis-theotokou-kardamena
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kos/#kardamena-panigiri-of-genesio-tis-theotokou-kardamena
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythnos-kanala-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiri-panagia-kanala-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Nativity of the Virgin panigiri\, Panagia Kanala
LOCATION:Kanala\, Kythnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kanala's second big feast\, for the Nativity of the Virgin\, with vespers on 7 September and liturgy on the 8th at the shrine\, plus the Kalolivadiani chapel at Kalo Livadi celebrating the same day. Quieter than 15 August and with September prices\, it's the better pick if you want the Kanala atmosphere without the crush — the beach below is still warm enough to swim.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#kanala-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiri-panagia-kanala
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythnos/#kanala-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiri-panagia-kanala
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:lemnos-saint-sozon-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270908
SUMMARY:Saint Sozon
LOCATION:Lemnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Patron saint of Lemnos. Pilgrimage to the church at Akti and surrounding panigiri.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#saint-sozon
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/lemnos/#saint-sozon
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-plaka-panigiri-of-panagia-korfiatissa-plaka-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Korfiatissa\, Plaka
LOCATION:Plaka\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Plaka's own feast\, for the Nativity of the Virgin at the cliff-edge church of Panagia Korfiatissa: vespers on the evening of 7 September\, then an island panigiri with live music in the central square of Plaka. Come early enough to watch the sunset from the church terrace first\; the square is small and fills fast\, and the whole village is on foot.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#plaka-panigiri-of-panagia-korfiatissa-plaka
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#plaka-panigiri-of-panagia-korfiatissa-plaka
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paros-marmara-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-marmara-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Faneromeni\, Marmara
LOCATION:Marmara\, Paros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Marmara\, the farming village next to Marpissa\, celebrates the Nativity of the Virgin at its church of Panagia Faneromeni with a liturgy on 8 September and a panigiri the evening before\, with food\, wine and island dancing in the square. A good\, unhurried September feast once the crowds have gone.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#marmara-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-marmara
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#marmara-panigiri-of-panagia-faneromeni-marmara
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:rhodes-archangelos-panigiri-of-panagia-tsambika-archangelos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Tsambika\, Archangelos
LOCATION:Archangelos\, Rhodes\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 7-8 September pilgrims climb the 300-odd steps to the tiny monastery of Panagia Tsambika on its rock above Kolymbia\; childless couples traditionally go up barefoot\, and children born after a vow are named Tsambikos or Tsambika\, which is why you meet so many of them on Rhodes. Vespers on the evening of the 7th\, liturgy on the 8th\, then food and music down at the lower monastery by the road. Go early\; the car park by the road fills by mid-morning.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#archangelos-panigiri-of-panagia-tsambika-archangelos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/rhodes/#archangelos-panigiri-of-panagia-tsambika-archangelos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:samos-vourliotes-feast-of-the-nativity-of-the-virgin-panagia-vront-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Feast of the Nativity of the Virgin\, Panagia Vrontiani monastery (Vourliotes)
LOCATION:Vourliotes\, Samos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Samos's oldest monastery (1566)\, above the mountain village of Vourliotes\, keeps its patronal feast with a hierarchical vespers on the evening of 7 September and liturgy and icon procession on the 8th\, presided by the Metropolitan of Samos. Pilgrims from the whole island come\; traditionally boiled meat with wheat is shared afterwards and the village square below fills for music. Narrow road\, so park in Vourliotes and walk the last stretch.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#vourliotes-feast-of-the-nativity-of-the-virgin-panagia-vront
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#vourliotes-feast-of-the-nativity-of-the-virgin-panagia-vront
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sifnos-exambela-panigiri-of-panagia-vrysiani-nativity-of-the-virgin-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Vrysiani (Nativity of the Virgin)\, Exambela
LOCATION:Exambela\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 17th-century Moni Vrysis below Exambela\, with its small ecclesiastical museum\, celebrates the Nativity of the Virgin with vespers and a monastery-table panigiri on the evening of 7 September — chickpea soup\, lamb\, wine and a takimi in the courtyard. It's a ten-minute walk down from Exambela village\; a good one to combine with a September stay in Apollonia when the island has calmed down.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#exambela-panigiri-of-panagia-vrysiani-nativity-of-the-virgin
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#exambela-panigiri-of-panagia-vrysiani-nativity-of-the-virgin
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:skyros-achilli-panigiri-of-panagia-lymbiani-and-panagia-spiliotissa-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Lymbiani and Panagia Spiliotissa (8 September)
LOCATION:Achilli\, Skyros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Nativity of the Virgin is kept on 7-8 September at Panagia Lymbiani and on the 8th at the cave chapel of Panagia Spiliotissa above Achilli bay south of the Chora\, with tavles after the liturgy. Good late-season option: warm sea\, empty beaches and the last violins of the year.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skyros/#achilli-panigiri-of-panagia-lymbiani-and-panagia-spiliotissa
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/skyros/#achilli-panigiri-of-panagia-lymbiani-and-panagia-spiliotissa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:syros-pagos-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiria-chroussa-and-pagos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270907
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Nativity of the Virgin panigiria\, Chroussa and Pagos
LOCATION:Pagos\, Syros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:On 7-8 September the Catholic villages of the interior celebrate the Nativity of the Virgin: Pagos and Chroussa with a liturgy and a square panigiri with violin\, laouto and local food\, and Lotos and Voulias (Kini) at their own chapels of the Virgin over the following days. Pagos also has a well-known island evening in late July.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/syros/#pagos-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiria-chroussa-and-pagos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/syros/#pagos-nativity-of-the-virgin-panigiria-chroussa-and-pagos
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:spetses-armata-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270908
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270909
SUMMARY:Armata
LOCATION:Spetses\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The single most spectacular naval festival in Greece. Reenacts the 1822 Battle of Spetses — a wooden replica of the Ottoman flagship is set ablaze in the harbour\, with fireworks. Hundreds of thousands attend\; book accommodation months ahead.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#armata
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/spetses/#armata
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:donousa-stavros-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-stavros-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270915
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Holy Cross\, Stavros
LOCATION:Stavros\, Donousa\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The village is named for its church of the Holy Cross\, so 13-14 September is Stavros's own feast: vespers\, liturgy and a smaller repeat of the August panigiri with local food\, music and dancing\, at the end of the season when only islanders and a few stragglers are left.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/donousa/#stavros-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-stavros
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/donousa/#stavros-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-stavros
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:folegandros-chora-panigiri-of-stavros-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270915
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Stavros\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Folegandros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The Exaltation of the Cross is kept in Chora on the evening of 13 September with a glenti in Plateia Agiou Nikolaou — food and wine put out by residents\, violin and laouto and the locals' own dancing. September is the sweet spot on Folegandros: warm sea\, empty beaches\, and this is the last feast before the island winds down.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#chora-panigiri-of-stavros-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/folegandros/#chora-panigiri-of-stavros-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paros-agkairia-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-stavros-agkairia-and-ali-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270915
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Holy Cross (Stavros)\, Agkairia and Aliki
LOCATION:Agkairia\, Paros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:For the Exaltation of the Cross the parish of Agkairia holds its liturgy with kerasmata afterwards\, and in the evening the dance groups perform and the tables come out down on the seafront at Aliki. It is the last of the summer panigiria in the south of the island.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#agkairia-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-stavros-agkairia-and-ali
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#agkairia-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-stavros-agkairia-and-ali
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:samos-mytilinioi-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-mytilinioi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270915
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Holy Cross\, Mytilinioi
LOCATION:Mytilinioi\, Samos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Once 'the largest panigiri in the area'\, the Stavros feast of Mytilinioi has been revived by the village association and is held on the eve\, 13 September\, from 20:00 in the central square with the village's traditional musicians. The Cross is also kept on 14 September at Mavratzaioi and the Timiou Stavrou monastery nearby. Late-season\, mostly Samians.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#mytilinioi-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-mytilinioi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/samos/#mytilinioi-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-mytilinioi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:santorini-emporio-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-stavros-emporio-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270915
SUMMARY:Panigiri of the Holy Cross (Stavros)\, Emporio
LOCATION:Emporio\, Santorini\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Emporio\, the big medieval village in the south\, celebrates the Exaltation of the Cross on 13-14 September with a liturgy and a panigiri in the square: local wine\, food\, music and dancing. Mid-September is grape-harvest time\, so the wine is new and the village is in a good mood.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/santorini/#emporio-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-stavros-emporio
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/santorini/#emporio-panigiri-of-the-holy-cross-stavros-emporio
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sifnos-faros-panigiri-of-timios-stavros-faros-and-choni-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270915
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Timios Stavros\, Faros and Choni
LOCATION:Faros\, Sifnos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Two Stavros feasts on the evening of 13 September: at Fasolou by Faros beach\, and at Choni on the road to Cheronissos. Both follow the Sifnos formula — vespers\, then the panigyras's revithada and lamb at long tables\, violin and laouto. Faros is the one to choose if you're without a car\; Choni is quieter and more local.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#faros-panigiri-of-timios-stavros-faros-and-choni
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sifnos/#faros-panigiri-of-timios-stavros-faros-and-choni
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:sikinos-chora-panigiri-of-stavros-chora-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270913
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270915
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Stavros\, Chora
LOCATION:Chora\, Sikinos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:For the Exaltation of the Cross the sponsoring family gives an evening meal for the village on 13 September and\, as with every Sikinos feast\, takes the icon home for a year. It's a quiet\, entirely local evening at the end of the season — the sort of thing you stumble on rather than plan around\, but worth knowing if you're on the island in mid-September.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sikinos/#chora-panigiri-of-stavros-chora
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/sikinos/#chora-panigiri-of-stavros-chora
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:meganisi-vathy-feast-of-agios-vissarion-patron-of-meganisi-vathy-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270915
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270916
SUMMARY:Feast of Agios Vissarion\, patron of Meganisi\, Vathy
LOCATION:Vathy\, Meganisi\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Agios Vissarion is Meganisi's protector and 15 September is the island's own feast day: the Metropolitan of Lefkada usually comes over to lead the liturgy in Vathy\, followed by a procession of the icon to the harbour and a reception. The island has emptied of tourists by then\, so it is the most Meganisiot day of the year\; ferries from Nydri run as normal.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/meganisi/#vathy-feast-of-agios-vissarion-patron-of-meganisi-vathy
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/meganisi/#vathy-feast-of-agios-vissarion-patron-of-meganisi-vathy
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:donousa-mersini-panigiri-of-agia-sofia-mersini-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270916
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270918
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Sofia\, Mersini
LOCATION:Mersini\, Donousa\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The spring village of Mersini\, with its plane tree and view down to Livadi beach\, celebrates its church of Agia Sofia in mid-September with a liturgy and a meal and music in the courtyard. The church calendar puts Agia Sofia on 17 September\, though local listings give 19 September\, so confirm at the port when you arrive.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/donousa/#mersini-panigiri-of-agia-sofia-mersini
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/donousa/#mersini-panigiri-of-agia-sofia-mersini
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ikaria-monokampi-panigiri-of-agia-sofia-monokampi-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270917
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270918
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Sofia\, Monokampi
LOCATION:Monokampi\, Ikaria\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The 'big panigiri' of Monokampi\, a village under plane trees on the south coast road between Agios Kirykos and Manganitis\, on 17 September from midday: local meat\, Ikarian wine and the Aganta band in 2025. September is when Ikarians themselves go to panigiria\, so this is one of the most authentic on the calendar. Kampos on the north side also keeps Agia Sofia this day.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#monokampi-panigiri-of-agia-sofia-monokampi
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/ikaria/#monokampi-panigiri-of-agia-sofia-monokampi
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythira-agia-pelagia-panigiri-on-the-eve-of-panagia-myrtidiotissa-ag-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270925
SUMMARY:Panigiri on the eve of Panagia Myrtidiotissa\, Agia Pelagia
LOCATION:Agia Pelagia\, Kythira\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The evening before the island's great feast of the Myrtidiotissa (24 September) the port village of Agia Pelagia holds its annual chorós on the waterfront from 9pm\, with a live band\, food and dancing\, before everyone drives across to the Myrtidia monastery for the vigil and morning liturgy. Late September is warm and the island is quiet again\; a good weekend to see Kythira as the Kythirans do.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythira/#agia-pelagia-panigiri-on-the-eve-of-panagia-myrtidiotissa-ag
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythira/#agia-pelagia-panigiri-on-the-eve-of-panagia-myrtidiotissa-ag
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:patmos-agriolivado-panigiri-of-agia-thekla-agriolivado-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270925
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agia Thekla\, Agriolivado
LOCATION:Agriolivado\, Patmos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The last panigiri of the Patmos summer: on the evening of 23 September boats cross from Agriolivado to the little chapel of Agia Thekla on the islet opposite for vespers\, treats\, and then food and song on the beach. Small and very local.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/patmos/#agriolivado-panigiri-of-agia-thekla-agriolivado
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/patmos/#agriolivado-panigiri-of-agia-thekla-agriolivado
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:santorini-kamari-panigiri-of-panagia-myrtidiotissa-kamari-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270923
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270925
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Panagia Myrtidiotissa\, Kamari
LOCATION:Kamari\, Santorini\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kamari's parish church of Panagia Myrtidiotissa celebrates on 24 September\, with vespers the evening before and a panigiri with wine\, food\, music and dancing for the beach village at the end of its season. Easy to reach by bus from Fira.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/santorini/#kamari-panigiri-of-panagia-myrtidiotissa-kamari
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/santorini/#kamari-panigiri-of-panagia-myrtidiotissa-kamari
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:kythira-panagia-myrtidiotissa-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270924
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270925
SUMMARY:Panagia Myrtidiotissa
LOCATION:Kythira\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Kythira's biggest day. The miraculous icon — found in a myrtle bush in the 14th century — draws over a thousand pilgrims to the Myrtidia monastery. After the 9am liturgy the icon is carried in procession around the grounds behind the Potamos brass band\, with sweets and coffee handed out to everyone. Also marked on 15 August.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythira/#panagia-myrtidiotissa
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/kythira/#panagia-myrtidiotissa
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:milos-chalakas-panigiri-of-ai-giannis-siderianos-chalakas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270927
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Ai-Giannis Siderianos\, Chalakas
LOCATION:Chalakas\, Milos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The last big feast of the Milos season\, for Agios Ioannis Theologos 'Siderianos' at the old monastery in the wild south-west (Chalakas). The icon is brought over from the Korfiatissa church with honours\, and the village and the church committee lay on a glenti with island musicians in the courtyard\; the party is usually held on the Saturday nearest the feast (20 Sept 2025\, 21 Sept 2024) with vespers on 25 September\, so check milosvoice.gr for the exact night. Hundreds come\, including Kimolians\; the road in is unpaved for the last stretch.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#chalakas-panigiri-of-ai-giannis-siderianos-chalakas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/milos/#chalakas-panigiri-of-ai-giannis-siderianos-chalakas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:mykonos-diakofti-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-diakofti-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270927
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Theologos\, Diakofti
LOCATION:Diakofti\, Mykonos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The hill chapel of Agios Ioannis at Diakofti celebrates the Theologian on 26 September (and again on 8 May) with a family-run panigiri: vespers\, then lamb\, wine and tsambouna music for whoever climbs up. September on Mykonos is when the old island reappears\, and this is a good place to see it.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#diakofti-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-diakofti
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/mykonos/#diakofti-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-diakofti
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:naxos-apollonas-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-apollonas-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270927
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Theologos\, Apollonas
LOCATION:Apollonas\, Naxos\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The fishing village of Apollonas at the northern tip celebrates St John the Theologian twice\, on 8 May and 26 September\, with grilled meat and seafood\, local wine\, music and dancing by the harbour. The September one is the last panigiri of the Naxos season\, with the tourists gone and the water still warm.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#apollonas-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-apollonas
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/naxos/#apollonas-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-apollonas
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:nisyros-nikia-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-nikia-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270927
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Theologos\, Nikia
LOCATION:Nikia\, Nisyros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:The monastery of Agios Ioannis Theologos just below Nikia\, the village on the crater rim\, has its feast on 25-26 September: vespers\, food in the courtyard and dancing to violin and laouto. Late season\, so a good excuse to see the volcano with few people around.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/nisyros/#nikia-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-nikia
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/nisyros/#nikia-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-nikia
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:paros-dryos-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-dryos-2027@aegeanblueprint.com
DTSTAMP:20260902T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20270925
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20270927
SUMMARY:Panigiri of Agios Ioannis Theologos\, Dryos
LOCATION:Dryos\, Paros\, Greece
DESCRIPTION:Dryos on the south-east coast keeps the autumn feast of St John the Theologian (26 September) with a panigiri on the evening of the 25th from about 21:00: local food\, wine and island music and dance groups by the harbour. The same chapel also celebrates on 8 May with a smaller gathering.\n\nhttps://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#dryos-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-dryos
URL:https://aegeanblueprint.com/festivals/paros/#dryos-panigiri-of-agios-ioannis-theologos-dryos
END:VEVENT
